  <title id="bdl08irislaplace-title">Last-layer Laplace classification of two Iris species</title>
  <desc id="bdl08irislaplace-desc">Four heat maps over sepal width from 1.9 to 3.95 centimeters and petal width from 0.9 to 2.6 centimeters, each overlaid with the 100 versicolor (open markers) and virginica (filled markers) flowers, with circles for training, triangles for validation and squares for test points. In panels a to c the accent shading gives the probability of virginica: the MAP panel switches sharply from light at small petal width to dark at large petal width, while the Monte Carlo and probit panels show the same boundary with a broader, softer transition that fades toward intermediate shading away from the data, and the two are nearly identical. Panel d shades the predictive entropy, which is highest along the class boundary and away from the data and lowest in the two class clusters.</desc>
